WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
The space shuttle Challenger disaster&nbsp;
could be traced to ONE mistake:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.780
the failure of these black rubber bands.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.020
They were meant to seal the&nbsp;
right solid rocket booster joint.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:15.660
The O-rings were supposed to move into the&nbsp;
groove to prevent the hot gases from leaking.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.160
But the cold weather caused both the&nbsp;
primary and backup O-ring to stiffen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.560
so they failed to stop the gas from escaping.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:28.320
To test this theory, scientist Richard Feynman&nbsp;
dunked a rubber O-ring into a glass of ice water.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.540
Clip It doesn’t stretch back; it stays the same&nbsp;
dimension. I believe that has some significance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:35.880
for our problem.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.900
This discovery put Feynman on&nbsp;
the map. For the full video on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.660
his incredible life, the link is in my comments.

